Chapter: QuotesParse

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as SortAscending
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "30a23f41fc17ec2aac012d0755750484a535afbcff80882094d569bbc7bdefff" 10000
  trusting above 5000

 What this pins is that the header parses -- that a chapter may cite,
 quote, pin a trusted key and set a floor in the same breath -- and that
 the trusted-key form lexes and means what it says: a fingerprint, the
 public key its signatures verify against, and a score. The quoted work
 is admitted because THIS source vouches for its signer, and doubled
 below is the chapter's own, untouched by any of it.

 It also pins that quotes, trusting and above are real keywords: this
 chapter would not lex without them.

Section: Body

  doubled : Integer -> Integer
  doubled (n) = n * 2

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("doubled=" & show (doubled 21))
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

%%QUOTED-WORKS%%
WORK 71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b alice 1000 fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff 311df63c5138f9b45671083a37a375c5e73ce536001fb337e8c6ac6b27a5ba05f1fe00613b7bf4dcaaee83e24d8e43b712e2d17c4e3d542b1c455ddc97d1d00a 6
Chapter: Sorted

Section: Body

  sort-ascending : Integer -> Integer
  sort-ascending (n) = n + 100
